    "result_text": "The change is complete and all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI updated `AssignCustomerCode.java` to de-duplicate the computed `customerCode` against existing owners.\n\n**What changed** (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignCustomerCode.java`):\n\n- Injected `OwnerRepository` into the `service` method (resolved by type, per the OfficeFloor function-injection convention used elsewhere, e.g. `CountNamesakes`).\n- After computing the base `<REGION>-<HASH8>` code, it gathers the set of existing owners' `customerCode` values via `findAll()`.\n- If the base collides, it appends `-<n>` with the smallest `n \u2265 2` that is unique (`base-2`, `base-3`, \u2026); otherwise the bare base is kept.\n- Updated the Javadoc to document the de-duplication rule.\n\nSince this step already runs under `govern: [ transaction ]` before `SaveOwner`, and after telephone normalization, the collision check sees committed owners and the hash is stable.\n\n**Tests:** The full suite (`AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodesStayUnique`, which asserts distinct owners always get distinct customer codes) passes \u2014 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
